Hello MiNTOS users!

I am back again, with slightly enhanced version of ttyvdev - virtual consoles
(originally created by Juergen Lock). This release has two important new
features: new character attributes and Falcon enhanced resolution.

If you're Falcon user, please read the README.Falcon info file to find
out how to set up your favourite resolution in vconsoles.

The new character attributes are italic (skewed) and dim. The support
for these was in vconsoles for some time, but the codes for enabling
and disabling them was not there. I introduced four new ESC codes:

ESCm enters dim mode
ESCn exits dim mode

ESCr enters italic mode
ESCs exits italic mode

So now vconsoles support five special font font attributes: reverse,
underline, bold, dim and italic. Just type 'cat testtext' and you'll
see the effects on your screen.

When I was writting termcap and terminfo support for these new modes,
I needed to solve one problem: italic mode is not defined by termcap
nor terminfo as no VGA card nor text terminal supports italic.
OTOH, both databases support BLINK mode (blinking text), which is
(nearly) impossible on our graphics terminals. So I defined italic
mode as BLINK attribute in termcap and terminfo databases.

New vconsoles are just great - the new attributes are very useful
for example in text editor 'elvis', which does syntax-highlightening
for C source code. So now I have C keywords in bold, C comments in
dim and text strings are underlined. The C source code is much
easier to read now. You can try it out yourself - elvis 2.0 for MiNT
is on my WWW home page.

EnJoy vconsoles.

